====== gfg Find nth root of m =======

Link --> https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/find-nth-root-of-m5843/1


Step-by-step algorithm to find the nth root of a number m using Binary Search:

Step 1: Initialize two variables:

* low = 0
* high = m

Step 2: Repeat the following steps while low is less than or equal to high.

Step 3: Find the middle value:

* mid = low + (high - low) / 2

Step 4: Compute mid raised to the power n.

* Initialize power = 1
* Multiply power by mid, n times
* If at any point power becomes greater than m, stop early

Step 5: Compare the calculated power with m.

* Sub-step 5a: If power is equal to m,
  return mid because mid is the nth root.

* Sub-step 5b: If power is greater than m,
  move the search space to the left side by setting
  high = mid - 1

* Sub-step 5c: If power is less than m,
  move the search space to the right side by setting
  low = mid + 1

Step 6: Continue this process until low becomes greater than high.

Step 7: If no value satisfies mid^n = m, return -1.

Time Complexity:
Binary search runs in log m steps.
Inside each step, power calculation runs n times.
Time Complexity = O(n × log m)

Space Complexity:
Only a few variables are used.
Space Complexity = O(1)



            ------------------> Code <--------------------

class Solution {
    public int nthRoot(int n, int m) {
        int low=0, high=m;
        while(low<=high){
            int mid=low+(high-low)/2;
            long power=1;
            
            for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
                power*=mid;
                if(power>m)break;
            }
            
            if(power==m){
                return mid;
            }else if(power>m){
                high=mid-1;
            }else{
                low=mid+1;
            }
            
        }
        return -1;
    }
}
